# BOOTSTRAP — agent entry gate

**Location:** this directory (`openOODA/`).  
**CWD:** `openOODA/` — all paths relative here. File is `BOOTSTRAP.oot` (upper).  
**Scope:** Process hub for agent work. Not product source.

## Where things live

| Tree | Role |
|------|------|
| `openOODA/` (here) | Process docs, swarm lanes, scripts index |
| `../ooda/` | Product code |
| `../std/` | Standard library |
| `../ooda/bootstrap/` | Residual packs — not law, except `CAPS_MATRIX.oot` when gating ops |
| `bootstrap/` (here) | Local honesty packs (e.g., `STDLIB_CRYPTO_MATH.oot`) |

## Tiered reads (not all every turn)

Load only what the turn needs.

| When | Read |
|------|------|
| **Always** | `RULES.oot`, `OODA.oot`, `LORE.oot`, `SWARM.oot` |
| Multi-agent / concurrent writes | `SPRINT.oot` §Lanes (folded `LANE.oot`) |
| Behavioral anti-patterns & Code Review | `SINS.oot` |
| Motivation & Architectural Philosophy | `SCIENCE.oot` |
| Hostile claim check / security falsification / fail-open hunt | `PROBE.oot` |
| Security, sandboxing, capability gating | `CAPS.oot` (catalog) + `../ooda/bootstrap/CAPS_MATRIX.oot` when gating ops |
| Product path / architecture | `DESIGN.oot` + **current goal** from `SPRINT.oot` or `PM.oot` (not the whole log) |
| Language / grammar / STE work | `DESIGN.oot` Appendix — Language Specification (folded `SPEC.oot`) |
| Automation / migration tools | `SCRIPTS.oot` |

Do not preload the full set "just in case." Token waste is a process defect.

## Docs format

- **New docs under `openOODA/`:** `.oot` only.
- **Global `.md` Ban:** The migration is complete. All docs across the org (`ooda/`, `std/`, `openOODA/`, `docs/`, `brand/`, `qa/`, `helloworld/`, `vscode/`, `tree-sitter/`, `openOODA.github.io/`, `.github/`) must use the `.oot` extension. Legacy `.md` files are forbidden.

## Done-bar (before product edits)

Before you change product code (`../ooda/`, `../std/`, or related trees), state in plain English:

1. **Active goal** — which sprint/PM item this turn serves.  
2. **Axiom** — which RULES principle binds the change (hygiene, fail-closed, security, E-M, etc.).

No goal + axiom → no product edit.

## Power law

Decide ≤ **5** work items per turn. Prefer one clear ship over a pile of half-starts.

## After bootstrap

Run the OODA loop (`OODA.oot`). Respect lane ownership (`SPRINT.oot` §Lanes — folded `LANE.oot`) so two write-agents never own the same file.
